{"name":"Daintree","hex":"#012731","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Daintree, Queensland","blocks":[{"text":"Daintree is a rural town and locality in the Shire of Douglas, Queensland, Australia. In the 2021 census, the locality of Daintree had a population of 93 people."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Daintree_29th_Feb.jpg/330px-Daintree_29th_Feb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daintree%2C_Queensland","wikidata":"Q4116524"},{"title":"Daintree River","blocks":[{"text":"The Daintree River is a river that rises in the Daintree Rainforest near Cape Tribulation in Far North Queensland, Australia. It flows into the Coral Sea. The river is part of the traditional lands of the Eastern Kuku Yalanji people, and is located about 100 kilometres (62 mi) northwest of Cairns in the UNESCO World Heritage–listed Wet Tropics of Queensland. Although this area is part of the Eastern Kuku Yalanji Native Title area, it is also a tourist attraction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/DaintreeRiverFerryOct242024_05.jpg/330px-DaintreeRiverFerryOct242024_05.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daintree_River","wikidata":"Q3012139"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/DaintreeConfluent.jpg/500px-DaintreeConfluent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/DaintreeConfluent.jpg/1280px-DaintreeConfluent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/DaintreeConfluent.jpg/500px-DaintreeConfluent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Confluent of tributary (foreground) and